     "what_changed": "That entry recorded the verdict '⭐ YES, AND IT STRENGTHENS THE ROUTE'S PREMISE' on the strength of two records. Re-read here against the four-category test, the verdict is WRONG AS STATED and right in a weaker form. Its first citation (PMID 36495678) asserts clientship in an INTRODUCTION and the same paper's own data are depletion, not binding; its second (PMID 24388362) is depletion-on-inhibition. NEITHER is a binding assay, and no binding assay for any FET fusion was found in this session's fifteen queries. The correct verdict is the one below: DEPENDENCE IS DOCUMENTED, CLIENTSHIP IS NOT. The 2026-08-09 record is left exactly as written — it is a dated retrieval, and corrections belong in an appendix rather than inline."
