-    "why_this_is_not_a_null_result_about_the_assay": "The assay exists and has been run on other fusion oncoproteins. AML1-ETO was shown to bind the chaperonin TRiC/CCT directly, by immunoprecipitation, mass spectrometry and cryo-EM, with HSP70 assistance and through its DNA-BINDING DOMAIN (PMID 26706127, PMID 27276256). So the absence of such a demonstration for any FET fusion is a genuine gap in the literature, not an artefact of the instrument."
+    "why_this_is_not_a_null_result_about_the_assay": "The assay exists and has been run on other fusion oncoproteins. AML1-ETO was shown to bind the chaperonin TRiC/CCT directly, by immunoprecipitation, mass spectrometry and cryo-EM, with HSP70 assistance and through its DNA-BINDING DOMAIN (PMID 26706127, PMID 27276256). So the fact that this search did not locate such a demonstration for a FET fusion is not explained by the instrument being unavailable. ⚠ It remains a gap in what this search retrieved, which is not the same as a gap in the literature: a negative or unpublished experiment would not appear here either. ⚠ Corrected 2026-09-08 (TD1 final review, root adjudication) F8."
