     "the_grade_should_not_move": "◐ PARTLY SUPPORTED is still right, and for the reason already written into it. This seat removes an over-read (the 'YES' of 2026-08-09) and adds one genuinely new positive (SGT1 knockdown destabilises EWS::FLI1, PMID 25985210) and one genuinely new negative (nothing exists for NR4A3 fusions at all). Those cancel: no clientship measurement has been added, and the expression-and-dependency reading the grade is built on is untouched.",
     "the_rationale_needs_one_correction": "⚠ RT-CHAPERONE's rationale says the chimera 'is a folding problem before it is a signalling one' because it joins two domains that never evolved together. The only fusion oncoprotein whose chaperone clientship HAS been solved structurally is handled through its DNA-BINDING DOMAIN (PMID 26706127), i.e. through the 3' partner's ordered fold, not through the disordered 5' prion-like half. If that generalises, the folding liability in EWSR1::NR4A3 would sit in the NR4A3 zinc-finger/ligand-binding region rather than in the EWSR1 low-complexity domain. That is a HYPOTHESIS generated by one comparator, not a finding.",
